<p>Three armed robbers entered a Crédit Agricole branch in Naples at about 11:30am on Thursday, held about 25 staff and customers hostage for roughly two hours, then escaped through a hole in the floor into a tunnel. Reports said they later vanished through the sewer system. The hostages were later released, and reports said no one was seriously hurt. The men appear to have targeted safe deposit boxes rather than carrying out a conventional cash robbery, and they escaped with loot before disappearing underground. The case has drawn attention in Italy because the escape route seems to have relied on Naples&#x27; underground infrastructure, making the search more difficult and raising new questions about how carefully the heist was planned.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/yAeyPB2gVlBxxpjwNxBRMgB6ANZYafOWyZhVjoVvB7p5ukPyDZfF7bkuylA4YwdgHegqv8lXQsocVsgTe2RBdFBrx-4w85Y8aIcORIOTSbMVlYBVIccGO3IpLifPDOCsWUWg2M10nB4qds-XUjqUa1cEA8URu53ImsK6E34DB8H5yARlz4BhMsW0jCRiyLg15StJEJ2MIsbyybWPoipxqZxj71I26gOxmMlXJVyk4Ep2fhXpFD7B2gSp_oPDoiYCUk3ho7z7VA2P1G-_Xg' alt='Scene outside the Naples bank branch after the hostage-taking and escape.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Escape route: Reports said the robbers likely used Naples&#x27; sewer system after disappearing through the bank floor, giving them a concealed way out of the area.</li><li>Targeted valuables: Reports said the thieves took items from safe deposit boxes, pointing to a planned search for customer valuables rather than teller cash.</li><li>Branch timing: The robbery began in the late morning, with The Guardian saying the trio entered the branch at about 11:30am.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Italian police: Officers searched for the robbers after the standoff. Reports said the men escaped through a tunnel and were believed to have used the sewer system. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c05d216rj85o'>BBC</a>)</li><li>Crédit Agricole branch customers and staff: The people inside the branch were held for about two hours before being released, making their safe recovery the immediate priority during the incident. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/16/armed-robbers-hostages-naples-bank-flee-hole-floor-sewers'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Media reporting from Naples: Coverage focused on three armed robbers who held about 25 people hostage inside the branch before escaping through underground infrastructure. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/news/638513-hostages-italy-naples-bank-heist/'>RT</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/bank-robbers-in-italy-hold-25-people-hostage'>Bank robbers in Italy hold 25 people hostage</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/638513-hostages-italy-naples-bank-heist/'>Dozens taken hostage in Italian bank heist (VIDEO)</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c05d216rj85o'>Naples bank robbers hold 25 people hostage then vanish through tunnel</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/16/armed-robbers-hostages-naples-bank-flee-hole-floor-sewers'>Armed robbers hold 25 people hostage at Naples bank before fleeing through hole in floor</a> - theguardian.com</li></ul>